# Build-time flags for the deployed build.
#
# VITE_DEMO_IDENTITY re-enables the seeded-person switcher and, with it, lets the
# application run on its bundled data when no API answers. That is what makes the
# deployment browsable: without it, every route redirects to a sign-in form that
# has no database to authenticate against.
#
# It is a deliberate, temporary trade. While it is set:
#
#   - anyone with the URL can open every screen, and
#   - anyone can take the place of any seeded person without a password.
#
# That is acceptable only because every record here is fictional — the salary
# figures are invented, the identity fields are placeholders, and the email
# addresses are at a domain that does not exist.
#
# Delete this line before the database is connected. Real records behind a
# passwordless switcher is the one thing this must never ship as.
VITE_DEMO_IDENTITY=true
